## Claim
Text: "Carlos Gimenez approved a 67% pay raise for himself and increased his own pension."
Claim author: Debbie Mucarsel-Powell
Claim date: September 17, 2020
Claim origin: https://www.debbiemucarselpowell.com/media-center/

## Initial Q&A
### Who is Carlos Gimenez and what public office or position did he hold at the time of the alleged action in 2020?
Answer: Carlos Gimenez was the Miami-Dade County Mayor at the time of the alleged action in 2020. The search result identifies him as the county mayor, first elected in 2011 and re-elected in 2012, responsible for leading the county's administration.

Source URL: https://miamilaker.com/Business/m-dade-mayor-carlos-gimenez-visits-ml-chamber

### What was Carlos Gimenez's annual salary before the alleged 67% pay raise?
Answer: Carlos Gimenez's annual salary before the alleged 67% pay raise was $150,000. As stated in the search result, "He brought the salary of $325,000 — which fueled the Carlos Alvarez recall as much as the Marlins stadium deal — down to $150,000."

Source URL: https://www.politicalcortadito.com/2018/09/21/salary-raise-mayor-carlos-gimenez/

### On what specific date or in what specific budget year was the pay raise for the position held by Carlos Gimenez approved?
Answer: The pay raise was approved as part of the Miami-Dade County budget approved by the county commission in September 2018, with the new salary taking effect in October 2018.

Source URL: https://www.politicalcortadito.com/2018/09/21/salary-raise-mayor-carlos-gimenez/

### Did Carlos Gimenez vote on or formally approve the legislation, budget, or policy that contained his own pay raise?
Answer: Based on the search result, Carlos Gimenez did not directly vote on or formally approve the legislation, as he was the mayor, not a member of the county commission. The source states that "the county commission approved a budget Thursday that includes the pay raise," and it notes that as strong mayor "he can apparently decide to give himself a raise whenever he wants," but the article does not describe him voting on or formally approving this specific measure himself.

Source URL: https://www.politicalcortadito.com/2018/09/21/salary-raise-mayor-carlos-gimenez/

### What was the exact percentage or dollar amount of the approved salary increase for Carlos Gimenez's position?
Answer: Carlos Gimenez received a $100,000-a-year raise, which the article describes as a "67% raise," nearly doubling his salary to $250,000 annually.

Source URL: https://www.politicalcortadito.com/2018/09/21/salary-raise-mayor-carlos-gimenez/

### Does the official record show the approved raise was indeed 67% as claimed?
Answer: The search result indicates that the county-approved budget set the mayor's salary maximum at $250,000, which is "$100K more than he makes right now" (his current salary being $150,000). This represents an increase of approximately 67% ($100,000/$150,000). However, the article notes that Mayor Gimenez was "coy" about whether he would apply the full budget maximum, stating he "may give money back," and it frames the potential raise as part of a strategy to inflate his pension.

Source URL: https://www.politicalcortadito.com/2018/09/22/3-reasons-why-carlos-gimenez-will-jack-his-salary-pension-suarez-mo-money/

### What were the specific changes to the pension plan or formula that resulted in an increased benefit for Carlos Gimenez?
Answer: The specific change was that Carlos Gimenez's increase in his salary to $250,000 for the last two years of his service directly raised the average of his highest five years of pay, which is a key component in the Florida Retirement System (FRS) pension formula for elected officials. As the source explains, "By jacking his own salary up $100,000 for the last two years to $250,000, he significantly improves that average," which in turn increases the calculated pension benefit, since the FRS formula uses "the average of the highest five or eight fiscal years of pay."

Source URL: https://www.politicalcortadito.com/2018/09/22/3-reasons-why-carlos-gimenez-will-jack-his-salary-pension-suarez-mo-money/

### Did the same official action that approved the salary increase also enact the pension benefit increase?
Answer: No, the source does not indicate that a single official action directly enacted both the salary increase and a separate pension benefit increase. Instead, it explains that the higher salary automatically improves his pension calculations under the Florida Retirement System's fixed formula, as "FRS pensions for elected officials are calculated... By jacking his own salary up... he significantly improves that average."

Source URL: https://www.politicalcortadito.com/2018/09/22/3-reasons-why-carlos-gimenez-will-jack-his-salary-pension-suarez-mo-money/

### What was the stated public rationale or justification provided by the governing body for approving this pay raise and pension change?
Answer: The request was rejected because it was considered high risk

